Graph schema source52-v1: nodes id/kind/contract/qualified_id/compiled52(false); edges ingredient -> consumer with kind/reason and exact caller_index0 or source_span when grounded in selected tokens/return fields. Mathematical obligation edges are explicitly unimplemented source-analysis ingredients, never claimed implementation calls. Future-consumer edges remain typed residuals.

Selected providers distinguish full public headers (stop strictly before :=), actual Measure.tilted definition body, exact bounded primary regions, and external-unexpanded primitive declaration-name token anchors (partial physical rows). Complete headers/bodies of primitives are outside selected scope; no recursive/whole-library expansion claimed. True class/name/field header anchors are NODE; no attribute-only false exclusion. Named namespace declaration labels are labels, not self-calls. Global Module is a true typing primitive; Module.finrank is distinct. CLM.comp is distinct from HasFDerivAt.comp. HasCompactSupport is attributed to its real additive generation source.

Coverage is exhaustive within exact selected raw UTF8 fragments, not all emitted locator context. Offset start0/end0exclusive; physical lines1-based. Lexical inventory covers every Unicode identifier plus listed analytic notation in selected Lean fragments; primary HTML markup is excluded from Lean lexical scan and exact alttext/href inventories retain mathematical formulas/source citations. Syntax punctuation/operator desugaring and primitive bodies are external boundaries. ∀ᵐ has separate actual ae-filter and Eventually references; explicit return-conjunct provenance is not an invented projection caller.

Raw SHA256 hashes physical bytes; LF SHA256 replaces CRLF with LF only. Native run hash is sorted compact UTF8 JSON of whole object minus run_sha256. Historical CLOSED leases/snapshots do not substitute for current own actual lease. Creator bookkeeping is byte enumeration only, not topology admission. No compiler/theorem claim/proof/implementation/shared write.
